{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101493","id":2273988734,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6HilB-","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101493","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101493.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101493.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101493","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101493/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101493/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101493/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/2e600789ddc12378df231358dae894a73b57c2ec","number":101493,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Optimize `String` `==`, `ends_with` and `begins_with` by using `memcmp`.","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This should behave identically as before.\r\n\r\n## Benchmark\r\nThe new implementation can be about 4x as fast as before:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\n\tString s1 = \"Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris nisi ut aliquip ex ea commodo consequat. Duis aute irure dolor in reprehenderit in voluptate velit esse cillum dolore eu fugiat nulla pariatur. Excepteur sint occaecat cupidatat non proident, sunt in culpa qui officia deserunt mollit anim id est laborum.\";\r\n\tString s2 = s1;\r\n\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\tfor (int i = 0; i < 10000000; i ++) {\r\n\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\tbool b = s1 == s2;\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t}\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\tfor (int i = 0; i < 10000000; i ++) {\r\n\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\tbool b = s1.begins_with(s2);\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t}\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tauto t0 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\tfor (int i = 0; i < 10000000; i ++) {\r\n\t\t\t// Test\r\n\t\t\tbool b = s1.ends_with(s2);\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tauto t1 = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();\r\n\t\tstd::cout << std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(t1 - t0).count() << \"ms\\n\";\r\n\t}\r\n```\r\n\r\n- `~1950ms` each on `master` (5b52b4b5c4f7c1232a6a814f65fce4c48f0f424b)\r\n- `~510ms` each on this PR (2e600789ddc12378df231358dae894a73b57c2ec)\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\nThis PR only optimizes string to string comparisons. It does not optimize comparison to string literals (which are `char[]`).\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://